<p><code>pop-mail</code> splits into two halves that share nothing but a namespace. A <code>Message</code> is composed and handed to a
<code>Mailer</code>, which hands it to a transport — SMTP, a hosted API, or <code>sendmail</code>. A client, separately, reads an
existing mailbox. Composing is the common case, and the transport is the only part that changes between a
laptop and production.</p>
